# T423h (ADR-0048 §1): two files under the std root declare `module std.dup`; `use std.dup.f` needs it, so the
# driver stops with AX_DRIVER_DUPLICATE_STD_MODULE naming the module path and both files (index order).
cmd: {compiler} check --std-root tests/modules/std_on_demand/fixtures/dup_std tests/modules/std_on_demand/fixtures/dup_main.ax
exit: 1
stderr-contains: AX_DRIVER_DUPLICATE_STD_MODULE
stderr-contains: std module `std.dup` is declared by both `tests/modules/std_on_demand/fixtures/dup_std/a/one.ax` and `tests/modules/std_on_demand/fixtures/dup_std/b/two.ax`
cache-inputs: tests/modules/std_on_demand
